        "original_id": "dfcbd7e5-5aa5-5796-b07d-cc99135f23d5",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Newark, Nottinghamshire, England\n- Organizations: UK Parliament, Conservative Party, Labour Party, Standards Committee\n- People: Robert Jenrick, Patrick Mercer, Fiona Jones\n- Roles: Member of Parliament, Independent MP\n- Events: 1997 general election, 2001 general election, 2014 Newark by-election, Patrick Mercer resignation\n\nFacts:\n- Fiona Jones was elected as Member of Parliament for Newark in Labour's landslide victory in the 1997 general election.\n- Patrick Mercer was elected as the Conservative Member of Parliament for Newark in the 2001 general election.\n- Patrick Mercer resigned the Conservative Party parliamentary whip in May 2013 after questions arose about paid advocacy.\n- Patrick Mercer served as an Independent Member of Parliament for Newark until resigning at the end of April 2014 after the Standards Committee suspended him for six months for a sustained and pervasive breach of the House's rules.\n- Robert Jenrick of the Conservative Party won the Newark seat in a by-election on 5 June 2014.\n- Newark is a constituency in Nottinghamshire, England, and it is currently represented in Parliament by Robert Jenrick.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
